---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import StoreButtons from "../components/StoreButtons.astro";
import MarkdownActions from "../components/MarkdownActions.astro";
import { REPOS } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="azula — peer to peer"
  description="Peer-to-peer chat, remote shells, and an LLM bridge over a direct, end-to-end encrypted iroh link."
  markdown="/index.md"
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Your peer, your shell, your LLM —<br />direct and end-to-end encrypted.</h1>
    <p>
      azula links two devices straight to each other over <a href="https://iroh.computer">iroh</a>: UDP
      holepunched, QUIC encrypted, no server in the middle. Chat with a peer, drive a remote shell, or
      push messages into an LLM session — all over the same direct link.
    </p>
    <div class="pill">◉ direct · 12ms · e2e</div>
    <StoreButtons />
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="glyph">z</div>
      <h3>peer chat</h3>
      <p>Paste a friend's code and you're talking over a direct, encrypted link. No account.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="glyph">✦</div>
      <h3>LLM via MCP</h3>
      <p>
        Connect an LLM through an MCP server on your own machine — it talks to your app, not a third
        party. <a href="/docs/mcp">Set it up →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="glyph">›_</div>
      <h3>remote shell</h3>
      <p>
        Hand a server's shell to your phone or desktop and drive it from anywhere.{" "}
        <a href="/docs/cli">See the CLI →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2>Start from the command line</h2>
    <p>
      One binary, no runtime. Start an MCP server and scan the pairing code it prints with the app —
      that pairs the whole machine, so every later session is admitted without another prompt.
    </p>
    <pre><code>azula mcp</code></pre>
    <p>Or drive it straight from a shell, no LLM involved:</p>
    <pre><code>azula message send --device phone "build finished"
azula run --handoff on-error -- make test</code></pre>
    <div class="btns">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/docs/install">Install the CLI</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2>Connecting an LLM to your session</h2>
    <p>
      Configure the azula MCP server once in any MCP-capable client — no per-session URLs. Then pair a
      device by giving azula its link (in chat, or <code>azula pair</code>):
    </p>
    <pre><code>https://azula.app/i/&lt;invite-payload&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      The same link works for a person — send it to a friend and it opens the app, or shows them how to
      join. <a href="/docs/links">How links work →</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2>Source</h2>
    <p>Every part of azula is on GitHub.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      {
        REPOS.map((repo) => (
          <div class="card">
            <div class="glyph">›_</div>
            <h3>
              <a href={repo.url} rel="noopener">
                {repo.name}
              </a>
            </h3>
            <p>{repo.blurb}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2>Readable by your agent</h2>
    <p>
      Every page here has a Markdown twin at the same path plus <code>.md</code>, indexed in
      <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> — or take the whole site as one document at
      <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a>.
    </p>
    <MarkdownActions href="/index.md" />
  </div>
</Base>
